Pre-requisites:
Make sure you have ubuntu wsl or gitbash. As of now I have Ubuntu WSL.

Steps:
1. Install docker and validate    //#docker version
2. Install kubectl                //#kubectl version --client
3. Install kind                   //#kind version
4. Create a cluster               //#kind create cluster, #kind create cluster --name mycluster --config kind-config.yaml
5. Verify Cluster                //#kubectl cluster-info
6. List cluster                 //#kind get clusters
7. Delete cluster                //#kind delete cluster ,#kind delete clusters --all

Create Multi-Node cluster from kind config file:
---
kind: Cluster
apiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4

nodes:
- role: control-plane
- role: worker
- role: worker
---
Verify the cluster details      //#kubectl get nodes  
